+
+  A continued session is held to the same bar: ownership is positional, so every line before the first own line with a `uuid` is a copy (Claude Code also copies lines without a `uuid`, such as `queue-operation`, that carry a timestamp and would otherwise set the summary's `started_at`), and until the session has activity of its own (`TranscriptParseState.continuationActive`) it reports no usage and no summary.
