+  **Claude Code's own OTel records.** The hook path is not the only one that moves a session: Claude Code posts its OTel exports (`hook_registered`, `plugin_loaded`, `mcp_server_connection`, ...) straight to the proxy daemon every time it opens a session, stamped with the time of the open. A session with an evidence record is forwarded even without hooks data, so these would reach the backend and move the session's end to the reopen. `otlp-spool/reopen-hold.ts` (`holdForIdleReopen`, called by `forwardSession` before the OTel streams) keeps every OTel stream of a session whose parse state is reopened and idle unsent, cursor untouched; they go out at the first pass that sees activity of its own, and are dropped unsent when the reopen stays idle past `OTLP_ABANDONED_SESSION_GRACE_MINUTES`. Bytes written after the session ended and before the resume hook has marked it are kept back for `OTLP_REOPEN_SETTLE_MINUTES` (default 15 s). The daemon reads the parse state without its lock; a stale read delays a release by one tick. Hooks without a pass of their own (`Notification`, `InstructionsLoaded`, ...) are dropped for the same idle reopen (`isSessionReopenedIdle`); a `UserPromptSubmit` marks the reopen active (`markReopenedActive`) so the hooks of its turn go out. Known limit: the backend's session binding for later activity from a different launch is not controllable from the CLI.
+
 **`UserPromptExpansion` / `agent.skill.dispatch`.** Only `slash_command` expansions are forwarded as skill dispatches. `mcp_prompt` expansions are ignored because they are not user slash-command skill invocations.
 
 **`agent.git.snapshot` commit times.** Each `git_commits[].time` is normalized to an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp ending in `Z`; `git_commits[].files` is the number of changed files, not a list of paths.
